COMBINATORIAL ANALYSIS (p.827)
24.3.3 Divisor Functions
I. Definitions
A. \sigma_{k}(n) is the sum of the k-th powers of the divisors of n. Often \sigma_{0}(n) is denoted by d(n), and \sigma_{1}(n) by \sigma(n).
B. Generating functions
\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{k}(n)n^{-s}=\zeta(s)\zeta(s-k)\quad\mathcal{D}g>k+1\]
\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{k}(n)x^{s}=\sum\limits_{n=1}^{n}\frac{r^{k}x^{s}}{1-x^{n}}\qquad|z|<1\]
C. Closed form
\sigma_{k}(n)=\sum\limits_{d\ln}d^{n}-\frac{t}{i=1}\frac{p_{1}^{k}a^{k+D}-1}{p_{1}^{k}-1}\qquad n=p_{1}^{k}p_{2}^{k}\dots\,p_{2}^{k}\]
II. Relations
A. Recurrences
\sigma_{k}(mn)=\sigma_{k}(m)\sigma_{k}(n)\qquad(m,\,n)=1
\sigma_{k}(np)=\sigma_{k}(n)\sigma_{k}(p)-p^{k}\sigma_{k}(n/p)\qquad p\text{ prime}
III. Asymptotics
\frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_{m=1}^{n}\sigma_{0}(m)=\ln n+2\gamma-1+O(n^{-1})
(\gamma=Euler's constant)
